      {
        "id": "F1",
        "severity": "WARNING",
        "location": "engine/settings/codegraph_prompt.go:24-27",
        "claim": "The wrapper is recognised only as the exact string for the current hookCommand. If the engine binary path changes between installs, the old wrapper is not recognised. If codegraph then rewrites the bare command, the next install adds a second, new-path wrapper beside the stale one. Both run, so codegraph may run twice per prompt, and the output of the old-path wrapper is not cleaned up. Uninstall with the new path also leaves the old-path wrapper, which keeps pointing at a binary that is gone.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "engine/settings/codegraph_prompt.go:24-27",
          "engine/settings/codegraph_prompt.go:113-120"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Reviewed the full diff. Wrapper matching in CodegraphPrompt and rewriteCodegraphPrompt uses strict equality against codegraphPromptWrapper(hookCommand), which embeds the binary path.",
      "Could not confirm from the diff how the existing hook families treat a UserPromptSubmit entry that contains the binary path; this is unknown."
